ation\nInternational mentoring programme\nDigital services\nArts and sport\nLibraries\nStudents with disabilities\nCatering services\nHealth and Well-being\nAbout\nAbout\nAbout us\nCampus maps\nEquality - Diversity - Inclusion - Disability\nThe Universit\u00e9 Paris-Saclay alumni network\nUniversit\u00e9 Paris-Saclay Scientific Framework\nGovernance\nMedia\nSearch\nMenu principal\nRetourner au haut de la page\nHome\nGraduate schools\nGraduate School Life Sciences and Health\nGraduate programs\nGraduate programs\nPrint this article\nShare\nTwitter\nFacebook\nLinkedin\nPar mail\nThe GS LSH enables synergies between Research-Teaching-Innovation actors and students by promoting exchanges between these communities within Graduate programs. The GS LSH is organized in 10 disciplinary and/or thematic graduate programs that bring together Master's and Doctoral programs and Research teams. In addition, a transverse MD-PhD type graduate program will be dedicated to obtaining both a PhD & a Doctorate degree in Medicine. The GS LSH is open internationally with 6 M1 and 15 M2 curriculums taught in English.\nDoctoral Schools\n1 - Structure and dynamics of living systems (SDSV) 2 - Neuroscience,Immunology, Endocrinology, Signal Transduction\n3 - Oncology, Biology, Medicine, Health (CBMS) 4 - Therapeutic Innovation: from the fundamental to the applied (ITFA)\n5 - Agriculture, Food, Biology, Environment, Health (ABIES) 6 - Plant sciences: from genes to ecosystems (SEVE)\nGraduate programs\nBiochemistry & Structural Biology\nResearch Teams\nBioinformatics\nResearch Teams\nBiotherapy & Oncology\nResearch Teams\nCell biology, Development, Aging,\nReproduction\nResearch Teams\nClinical Sciences\nResearch Teams\nEndocrinology, Biosignaling,\nMetabolism & Physiology\nResearch Teams\nEvolutionary biology\nResearch Teams\nGenetics & Genomics\nResearch Teams\nImmunology\nResearch Teams\nMicrobiology\nResearch Teams\nNeurosciences\nResearch Teams\nSystems & Synthetic biology\nResearch Teams\nM